        {
          "name": "idioms of \"kind\"",
          "displayOrder": 5,
          "viewType": "list",
          "partOfSpeech": null,
          "entries": [
            {
              "word": "in kind",
              "pronunciation": null,
              "entryType": "word",
              "notes": null,
              "displayOrder": 0,
              "definitions": [
                {
                  "text": "( of a payment 支付 ) consisting of goods or services, not money 以实物支付；以货代款；以服务偿付",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 0
                },
                {
                  "text": "( formal ) with the same thing 以同样的方法（或手段）",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 1
                }
              ],
              "examples": [
                {
                  "text": "She insulted him and he responded in kind. 她侮辱了他，他也以其人之道还治其人之身。",
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "images": []
            },
            {
              "word": "a kind of",
              "pronunciation": null,
              "entryType": "word",
              "notes": null,
              "displayOrder": 1,
              "definitions": [
                {
                  "text": "( informal ) used to show that sth you are saying is not exact （表示不确切）某种，几分，隐约",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "examples": [
                {
                  "text": "I had a kind of feeling this might happen. 我当时就隐约地感到会出这样的事。",
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "images": []
            },
            {
              "word": "kind of = kinda",
              "pronunciation": null,
              "entryType": "word",
              "notes": null,
              "displayOrder": 2,
              "definitions": [
                {
                  "text": "( informal ) slightly; in some ways 稍微；有几分；有点儿",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "examples": [
                {
                  "text": "That made me feel kind of stupid. 那使我感到有点儿愚蠢。",
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "images": []
            },
            {
              "word": "nothing of the kind/sort",
              "pronunciation": null,
              "entryType": "word",
              "notes": null,
              "displayOrder": 3,
              "definitions": [
                {
                  "text": "used to emphasize that the situation is very different from what has been said （强调情况与所说的大不相同）决不是那么回事，一点也不，才不哩；没有的事",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "examples": [
                {
                  "text": "'I was terrible!' 'You were nothing of the kind.' “我那时糟透了！”“你才不哩。”",
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "images": []
            },
            {
              "word": "of a kind",
              "pronunciation": null,
              "entryType": "word",
              "notes": null,
              "displayOrder": 4,
              "definitions": [
                {
                  "text": "( disapproving ) not as good as it could be 不怎么样，徒有其名（指不如本应有的那么好）",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 0
                },
                {
                  "text": "very similar 同一类的；类似的",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 1
                }
              ],
              "examples": [
                {
                  "text": "You're making progress of a kind. 你也算是有点进步的。",
                  "displayOrder": 0
                },
                {
                  "text": "They're two of a kind—both workaholics! 他们俩一个样—都是工作狂！",
                  "displayOrder": 1
                }
              ],
              "images": []
            },
            {
              "word": "one of a kind",
              "pronunciation": null,
              "entryType": "word",
              "notes": null,
              "displayOrder": 5,
              "definitions": [
                {
                  "text": "= unique",
                  "partOfSpeech": null,
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "examples": [
                {
                  "text": "My father was one of a kind—I'll never be like him. 我的父亲很独特—我决不会像他的。",
                  "displayOrder": 0
                }
              ],
              "images": []
            },
            {
